**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`

**How to implement.** The identities a setup is stored and referenced under, and the one dial rule its slots read, as pure Domain data (001 §J 'Setup = an ordered optical path of slots …; per slot: position on the beam, R1 / R2 / R3, or a dial reading'; 001 §J 'Experiments reference setups (name + revision)'; 001 §I 'Dial mapping: a rotatable item has a zero and a sign (DialSign exists). Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'; .spec-md §3.11, §5 'Setup, SetupName, slots'). Nothing reads them before step 256. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs`, on `DialSign` (moved there from `MuellerReconstruction.fs` by step 205): `member this.physicalAngleOf (zero : Angle) (reading : Angle) : Angle` is `Angle (this.value * (reading.value - zero.value))`, the rule `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:physicalAngle`) holds today, moved here: `physicalAngle`'s body becomes `analyzer.dialSign.physicalAngleOf analyzer.zeroDial dial`, its signature and doc kept and its doc saying the rule is `DialSign`'s, so the reference pipeline's numbers are unchanged. `member this.readingOf (zero : Angle) (angle : Angle) : Angle` is `Angle (zero.value + this.value * angle.value)`, the reading that gives `angle` (the sign is ±1, so it inverts `physicalAngleOf`). A reading is an `Angle` on the dial's scale, as `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle` already takes it; no reading type is added, so no wrap or bijection is introduced (ELEV001, ELEV006). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`. (a) Directly before step 221's `ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong`: `type FileStem with static member firstFreeText (text : string) (taken : FileStem list) : string` answers the first of `<text>`, `<text> (2)`, `<text> (3)`, … whose `FileStem.ofText` (step 24) no stem of `taken` equals ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`): the suffix sequence step 221 wrote into `ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong`, moved here, and `nextFreeAmong`'s body becomes the `ItemLabel` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` over the taken labels' `fileStem`s, so one sequence serves items and setups (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). A member may speak its type's primitives (AGENTS.md). (b) Appended at the end of the file, in this order, every case name of two words and no `bool`: `SetupError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the setup, the revision, the slot or the item: `InvalidSetupNameErr` (a blank name), `DuplicateSetupNameErr` (another setup of the kit has the name's file stem), `UnknownSetupErr` (the kit holds no setup of that name), `UnknownSetupRevisionErr` (the setup holds no such revision), `UnknownSetupSlotErr` (the table has no slot of that element), `UnknownSlotItemErr` (the kit holds no item of that id, or the library no model of it) and `IncompatibleSlotItemErr` (the item's model does not fit the slot's kind); `member this.describe : string` renders them `the setup name is not valid: <reason>`, `the kit already has a setup of that name: <reason>`, `the kit has no such setup: <reason>`, `the setup has no such revision: <reason>`, `the table has no such slot: <reason>`, `the item is not available: <reason>` and `the item does not fit the slot: <reason>`. `SetupName of string` with `.value`: `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<SetupName, SetupError>` keeps the text as given and refuses an empty or white-space text with `InvalidSetupNameErr`; `member this.fileStem : FileStem` is `FileStem.ofText this.value`, the stem of its `<name>.setup-json` (001 §A), so a name keeps the lab's characters (.spec-md §3.11, step 147's rule); `member this.nextFreeAmong (taken : SetupName list) : SetupName` is the `SetupName` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` over the taken names' `fileStem`s; `static member firstFree (taken : SetupName list) : SetupName` is the first of `Setup 1`, `Setup 2`, … whose `fileStem` no taken name has, ignoring case: the name a table takes when it becomes a setup without one (steps 261 and 264), until S8.3's template names setups from their slots. `SetupRevision of int` with `.value`, `static member first : SetupRevision` (1) and `member this.next : SetupRevision`. `SetupReference = { name : SetupName; revision : SetupRevision }`, one revision of one setup, with `member this.describe : string` = `'<name>' revision <n>`. No other type, member or option is added. Tests. In `KitTests` (step 122): `a setup name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`: `SetupName.tryCreate "CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL"` keeps the text and its `fileStem` is `FileStem "CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL"`; `"a: b/c"` has `FileStem "a_ b_c"`, equal to `FileStem.ofText "a: b/c"`; `""` and `"   "` answer `InvalidSetupNameErr`. `a setup takes the next free suffix of its name, and a table that is no setup yet takes the first free Setup n`: `(SetupName "Bench").nextFreeAmong [ SetupName "bench"; SetupName "Bench (2)" ]` is `SetupName "Bench (3)"`, among `[]` it is `SetupName "Bench"`, and `(SetupName "a:b").nextFreeAmong [ SetupName "a_b" ]` is `SetupName "a:b (2)"`; `SetupName.firstFree [ SetupName "Setup 1"; SetupName "setup 2" ]` is `SetupName "Setup 3"` and `SetupName.firstFree []` is `SetupName "Setup 1"`. `a setup revision starts at one and counts up, and a reference names its setup and revision`: `SetupRevision.first` is 1 and its `next.next` is 3, and `{ name = SetupName "Bench"; revision = SetupRevision.first.next }.describe` is `'Bench' revision 2`. `every setup error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. In `ItemModelsTests` (step 205): `a dial maps a raw reading to the physical angle by its sign and zero, and back`: `DialPositive.physicalAngleOf (10°) (40°)` is 30° and `DialNegative.physicalAngleOf (10°) (40°)` is −30°; for both signs and the angles −30°, 0°, 45° and 200°, `readingOf` of `physicalAngleOf` and `physicalAngleOf` of `readingOf` give the angle back within 1e-12; and `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle` of an `AnalyzerModel` with `dialSign = DialNegative` and `zeroDial = 10°` at 40° equals `DialNegative.physicalAngleOf (10°) (40°)` exactly. Step 221's `KitItemTests` facts on `ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong` pass unchanged, and `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests` keeps its numbers.

**Acceptance.** After the setup identities land, `SetupName`, `SetupRevision`, `SetupReference` and `SetupError` MUST exist in `Kit.fs` with the name, suffix and first-free rules, `DialSign.physicalAngleOf` MUST be the one dial rule that `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle` calls, and `FileStem.firstFreeText` MUST be the one suffix sequence; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a setup name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `a setup takes the next free suffix of its name, and a table that is no setup yet takes the first free Setup n`, `a setup revision starts at one and counts up, and a reference names its setup and revision`, `every setup error renders its condition and its payload` and `a dial maps a raw reading to the physical angle by its sign and zero, and back`, the count rising by 5; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests` with its numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
